---
import '@fontsource-variable/roboto-serif';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const updated = '28 August 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of use | Saielle DaSilva"
  description="The terms for using intentionaut.com and its newsletter."
>
  <section class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Terms of use</p>
      <h1>The short version.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        By using intentionaut.com or subscribing to the newsletter, you agree to
        what follows. It is deliberately brief.
      </p>
      <p class="article-meta">Last updated: {updated}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Who runs this</h2>
      <p>
        intentionaut.com is run by Intentionaut Ltd (Saielle DaSilva). Contact:
        <a href="mailto:hello@intentionaut.com">hello@intentionaut.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Using the site</h2>
      <p>
        Read it, link to it, quote from it with attribution and a link back. Do
        not republish whole pieces, pass the work off as your own, or scrape the
        site to train a model without asking me first. Ask; I am usually happy to
        say yes.
      </p>

      <h2>The writing is opinion, not advice for you</h2>
      <p>
        Everything here is my experience and my view. It is not tailored
        professional advice for your team or your situation, and decisions you
        make after reading it are your own.
      </p>

      <h2>No warranty</h2>
      <p>
        The site is provided as is. Links to other sites are not endorsements,
        and I am not responsible for their content.
      </p>

      <h2>The newsletter</h2>
      <p>
        Intentionaut is free and lands roughly every other week. There is no
        guaranteed schedule. You can unsubscribe at any time, and I may change or
        stop the newsletter whenever I choose.
      </p>

      <h2>Liability</h2>
      <p>
        As far as the law allows, I am not liable for any loss arising from using
        this site or acting on its content. Nothing here limits liability that
        cannot legally be limited.
      </p>

      <h2>Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts
        of England and Wales have jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>Updated terms and their date go here.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .article-meta {
    margin-top: var(--space-4);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .prose {
    padding-bottom: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem);
  }
</style>
